{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>By day</b> — He tells of his going by day with the festal crowd, trusting in HaShem's lovingkindness, and at night they would sing, like the bands of prophets. And he notes that the song is a prayer, not a song of desire." "<b>To a living El</b> — that He would keep him alive until he sees the House of YHWH."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "Resolved חשק as 'desire' (i.e., a secular love-song); the word could alternatively read as חשק meaning 'musical refrain,' but context favors the contrast with prayer."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:38.082077644Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}